{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01SEpUJdKNNdhQpp29m7VfSM","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Plan: Pipeline Round 0 Kernel Launches\n2\t\n3\t## Goal\n4\t\n5\tEliminate per-AIR GPU synchronization in the Round 0 constraint evaluation loop to allow the GPU to execute kernels back-to-back without CPU stalls. This targets the largest sub-component regression in \"STARK excl. trace\": Round 0 increases from 178ms (APC 0, 99 AIRs) to 662ms (APC 300, 623 AIRs) despite a >2x reduction in total cells and constraints.\n6\t\n7\t## Current Code Path\n8\t\n9\tThe bottleneck is in `sumcheck_uni_round0_polys()` at `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs:598-884`.\n10\t\n11\t**Call chain (per AIR iteration, lines 732-880):**\n12\t1. CPU: Prepare per-AIR data (constraints DAG, trace pointers, etc.)\n13\t2. `evaluate_round0_constraints_gpu()` at `round0.rs:31-124`:\n14\t   - Allocates `intermediates` (`DeviceBuffer::with_capacity`) — calls `cudaMallocAsync`\n15\t   - Allocates `temp_sums_buffer` (`DeviceBuffer::with_capacity`) — calls `cudaMallocAsync`\n16\t   - Allocates `sp_evals` output buffer\n17\t   - Launches `zerocheck_ntt_eval_constraints` kernel via FFI\n18\t   - Returns `sp_evals` DeviceBuffer (intermediates and temp_sums dropped = `cudaFreeAsync`)\n19\t3. **SYNC**: `sum_buffer.to_host()` at `mod.rs:792` — `cudaMemcpyAsync` + `cudaEventSynchronize`\n20\t4. CPU: Transpose, iDFT, polynomial construction → `batch_sp_poly[2*N + trace_idx]`\n21\t5. `evaluate_round0_interactions_gpu()` at `round0.rs:132-275`:\n22\t   - **CPU**: Builds `SymbolicDagBuilder`, encodes rules, computes numer/denom weights (lines 162-206)\n23\t   - Uploads `d_rules`, `d_numer_weights`, `d_denom_weights` to GPU (3 H2D copies)\n24\t   - Allocates `intermediates`, `temp_sums_buffer`, `s_evals` output buffer\n25\t   - Launches `logup_bary_eval_interactions_round0` kernel via FFI\n26\t   - Returns `s_evals` DeviceBuffer\n27\t6. **SYNC**: `sum.to_host()` at `mod.rs:848` — `cudaMemcpyAsync` + `cudaEventSynchronize`\n28\t7. CPU: Unzip frac, transpose, iDFT → `batch_sp_poly[2*i]`, `batch_sp_poly[2*i+1]`\n29\t\n30\t**Why this is slow with many AIRs:**\n31\t- 623 AIRs × 2 sync points = 1,246 GPU synchronizations via `cudaEventSynchronize`\n32\t- Each sync drains the GPU pipeline, preventing the next kernel from being submitted until the current one finishes AND the result is copied to host\n33\t- CPU work between syncs (DAG construction, iDFT, etc.) blocks kernel submission\n34\t- Per-AIR `cudaMallocAsync`/`cudaFreeAsync` for intermediates adds runtime API overhead\n35\t- All work runs on `cudaStreamPerThread` (per-thread default stream), so operations are serialized\n36\t\n37\t**Profiling evidence (APC 300):**\n38\t- Total GPU kernel time in Round 0: ~490ms (measured via nsight kernel summary)\n39\t- Measured Round 0 wall time: 662ms\n40\t- Overhead (sync stalls, CPU work, alloc): ~172ms (26% of wall time)\n41\t- Key kernels: `zerocheck_ntt_evaluate_constraints_coset_parallel_kernel` (220ms, 539 instances), `logup_r0_ntt_eval_interactions_coset_parallel_kernel` (195ms + 29ms, 735 instances)\n42\t\n43\t## Changes\n44\t\n45\t### Step 1: Extract interaction preparation from `evaluate_round0_interactions_gpu`\n46\t\n47\t**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/round0.rs`\n48\t\n49\tCreate a new struct and function to pre-compute per-AIR interaction data:\n50\t\n51\t```rust\n52\tpub struct InteractionRound0Prep {\n53\t    pub d_rules: DeviceBuffer<u128>,\n54\t    pub d_numer_weights: DeviceBuffer<EF>,\n55\t    pub d_denom_weights: DeviceBuffer<EF>,\n56\t    pub denom_sum_init: EF,\n57\t    pub buffer_size: u32,\n58\t}\n59\t```\n60\t\n61\tNote: The `SymbolicRulesGpu` is consumed during preparation (its `dag_idx_to_rule_idx` is used to map interaction expressions to rule indices for weight computation). Only the encoded device rules and computed weights survive into the struct. The `SymbolicDagBuilder` and its `expr_to_idx` map are also consumed during DAG construction and do not need to be stored.\n62\t\n63\tAdd function `prepare_round0_interactions(pk, symbolic, eq_3bs, beta_pows) -> Result<InteractionRound0Prep>` that extracts lines 161-212 from `evaluate_round0_interactions_gpu`. This performs:\n64\t- DAG construction via `SymbolicDagBuilder` (CPU)\n65\t- `SymbolicRulesGpu::new()` from the DAG (CPU)\n66\t- Rule encoding: `rules.rules.iter().map(|c| c.encode()).collect_vec()` (CPU)\n67\t- Weight computation: numer_weights, denom_weights, denom_sum_init using `rules.dag_idx_to_rule_idx` (CPU)\n68\t- H2D upload of encoded rules (`d_rules`) and weights (`d_numer_weights`, `d_denom_weights`)\n69\t\n70\t**Why**: Separates CPU-heavy preparation from kernel launch, allowing all preparation to be done upfront before any kernel launches.\n71\t\n72\t### Step 2: Create kernel-launch-only variants of the evaluation functions\n73\t\n74\t**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/round0.rs`\n75\t\n76\tAdd two new functions that take pre-allocated buffers and launch kernels without allocating or syncing:\n77\t\n78\t```rust\n79\tpub fn launch_round0_constraints_kernel(\n80\t    pk: &DeviceStarkProvingKey<...>,\n81\t    // ... same params as current evaluate_round0_constraints_gpu ...\n82\t    intermediates: &mut DeviceBuffer<F>,\n83\t    temp_sums: &mut DeviceBuffer<EF>,\n84\t    output: &mut DeviceBuffer<EF>,\n85\t) -> Result<(), Round0EvalError>\n86\t```\n87\t\n88\t```rust\n89\tpub fn launch_round0_interactions_kernel(\n90\t    prep: &InteractionRound0Prep,\n91\t    // ... trace pointers, eq_cube, etc ...\n92\t    intermediates: &mut DeviceBuffer<F>,\n93\t    temp_sums: &mut DeviceBuffer<Frac<EF>>,\n94\t    output: &mut DeviceBuffer<Frac<EF>>,\n95\t) -> Result<(), Round0EvalError>\n96\t```\n97\t\n98\tThese functions call the same FFI (`zerocheck_ntt_eval_constraints`, `logup_bary_eval_interactions_round0`) but use externally-owned buffers instead of allocating their own. They do NOT perform D2H copies.\n99\t\n100\t**Why**: Decouples kernel launch from allocation and sync, enabling pipeline execution.\n101\t\n102\t### Step 3: Restructure the main loop in `sumcheck_uni_round0_polys`\n103\t\n104\t**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs` (lines 720-884)\n105\t\n106\tReplace the single per-AIR loop with three phases:\n107\t\n108\t**Phase A — Prepare (CPU, before any kernel launches):**\n109\t```rust\n110\t// Pre-compute per-AIR metadata\n111\tlet mut per_air_data: Vec<Round0AirData> = Vec::with_capacity(num_present_airs);\n112\tfor (trace_idx, ...) in izip!(...).enumerate() {\n113\t    let single_pk = &self.pk.per_air[*air_idx];\n114\t    let symbolic = SymbolicConstraints::from(&single_pk.vk.symbolic_constraints);\n115\t    let local_deg = single_pk.vk.max_constraint_degree as usize;\n116\t    let num_cosets_zc = local_deg.saturating_sub(1);\n117\t    let num_cosets_logup = local_deg;\n118\t\n119\t    // IMPORTANT: max_constraint_degree includes interaction expression degrees.\n120\t    // An AIR can have num_cosets_zc > 0 but no plain AIR constraints.\n121\t    // We must check constraint_idx.is_empty() to determine if the zerocheck kernel\n122\t    // should be launched, matching the guard at round0.rs:46.\n123\t    let has_constraints = !single_pk.vk.symbolic_constraints.constraints.constraint_idx.is_empty()\n124\t        && num_cosets_zc > 0;\n125\t    \n126\t    // Build interaction prep (currently done inside the loop at round0.rs:161-206)\n127\t    let has_interactions = !eq_3bs.is_empty();\n128\t    let interaction_prep = if has_interactions {\n129\t        Some(prepare_round0_interactions(single_pk, &symbolic, eq_3bs, &self.beta_pows)?)\n130\t    } else { None };\n131\t    \n132\t    // Compute main_parts, preprocessed_ptr (same as current lines 763-768)\n133\t    let d_main_parts = ...;\n134\t    \n135\t    per_air_data.push(Round0AirData {\n136\t        air_idx, n, height, local_deg, num_cosets_zc, num_cosets_logup,\n137\t        has_constraints, has_interactions,\n138\t        interaction_prep, d_main_parts, omega_root, eq_xi_ptr, ...\n139\t    });\n140\t}\n141\t\n142\t// Pre-allocate shared intermediate buffers (max size across all AIRs).\n143\t// The sizing functions are thin wrappers over the existing unsafe FFI calls:\n144\t//   _zerocheck_r0_intermediates_buffer_size(buffer_size, skip_domain, num_x, num_cosets, max_temp_bytes)\n145\t//   _zerocheck_r0_temp_sums_buffer_size(buffer_size, skip_domain, num_x, num_cosets, max_temp_bytes)\n146\t//   _logup_r0_intermediates_buffer_size(buffer_size, skip_domain, num_x, num_cosets, max_temp_bytes)\n147\t//   _logup_r0_temp_sums_buffer_size(buffer_size, skip_domain, num_x, num_cosets, max_temp_bytes)\n148\t// For zerocheck, buffer_size comes from pk.other_data.zerocheck_round0.inner.buffer_size.\n149\t// For logup, buffer_size comes from InteractionRound0Prep.buffer_size.\n150\tlet max_zc_intermed = per_air_data.iter().map(|d| zc_intermediates_size(d)).max().unwrap_or(0);\n151\tlet max_zc_temp = per_air_data.iter().map(|d| zc_temp_size(d)).max().unwrap_or(0);\n152\tlet max_logup_intermed = per_air_data.iter().map(|d| logup_intermediates_size(d)).max().unwrap_or(0);\n153\tlet max_logup_temp = per_air_data.iter().map(|d| logup_temp_size(d)).max().unwrap_or(0);\n154\tlet mut zc_intermediates = DeviceBuffer::with_capacity(max_zc_intermed.max(1));\n155\tlet mut zc_temp_sums = DeviceBuffer::with_capacity(max_zc_temp.max(1));\n156\tlet mut logup_intermediates = DeviceBuffer::with_capacity(max_logup_intermed.max(1));\n157\tlet mut logup_temp_sums = DeviceBuffer::with_capacity(max_logup_temp.max(1));\n158\t\n159\t// Pre-allocate per-AIR output buffers (only for AIRs that will actually launch kernels)\n160\tlet mut zc_outputs: Vec<DeviceBuffer<EF>> = per_air_data.iter()\n161\t    .map(|d| if d.has_constraints { DeviceBuffer::with_capacity(d.num_cosets_zc * skip_domain) } else { DeviceBuffer::new() })\n162\t    .collect();\n163\tlet mut logup_outputs: Vec<DeviceBuffer<Frac<EF>>> = per_air_data.iter()\n164\t    .map(|d| if d.has_interactions { DeviceBuffer::with_capacity(d.num_cosets_logup * skip_domain) } else { DeviceBuffer::new() })\n165\t    .collect();\n166\t```\n167\t\n168\t**Phase B — Launch all kernels (no sync):**\n169\t```rust\n170\tfor (trace_idx, data) in per_air_data.iter().enumerate() {\n171\t    // Launch zerocheck constraint kernel ONLY if this AIR has plain constraints\n172\t    // (has_constraints checks both constraint_idx.is_empty() and num_cosets_zc > 0)\n173\t    if data.has_constraints {\n174\t        launch_round0_constraints_kernel(\n175\t            &self.pk.per_air[data.air_idx], data.selectors, &data.d_main_parts,\n176\t            data.public_values, data.eq_xi_ptr, d_lambda_pows,\n177\t            skip_domain, data.num_x, data.height, data.num_cosets_zc,\n178\t            data.omega_root, max_temp_bytes,\n179\t            &mut zc_intermediates, &mut zc_temp_sums, &mut zc_outputs[trace_idx],\n180\t        )?;\n181\t    }\n182\t    // Launch logup interaction kernel if this AIR has interactions\n183\t    if let Some(prep) = &data.interaction_prep {\n184\t        launch_round0_interactions_kernel(\n185\t            prep, data.selectors, &data.d_main_parts,\n186\t            data.public_values, data.eq_xi_ptr,\n187\t            skip_domain, data.num_x, data.height, data.num_cosets_logup,\n188\t            data.omega_root, max_temp_bytes,\n189\t            &mut logup_intermediates, &mut logup_temp_sums, &mut logup_outputs[trace_idx],\n190\t        )?;\n191\t    }\n192\t}\n193\t// All kernels submitted. No to_host() calls above.\n194\t```\n195\t\n196\t**Phase C — Sync once + batch process results:**\n197\t```rust\n198\t// Explicit stream sync before D2H copies using the existing safe wrapper\n199\t// (crates/cuda-common/src/stream.rs:81). This is cleaner than relying on the\n200\t// first to_host()'s event sync and avoids the COPY_EVENT mutex for the initial wait.\n201\tcurrent_stream_sync()?;\n202\t\n203\tfor (trace_idx, data) in per_air_data.iter().enumerate() {\n204\t    // Process zerocheck output (same logic as current lines 791-826)\n205\t    if !zc_outputs[trace_idx].is_empty() {\n206\t        let q_evals = zc_outputs[trace_idx].to_host()?;\n207\t        // ... transpose, iDFT, compute sp_0 ...\n208\t        batch_sp_poly[2 * num_present_airs + trace_idx] = UnivariatePoly::new(coeffs);\n209\t    }\n210\t    // Process logup output (same logic as current lines 847-878)\n211\t    if !logup_outputs[trace_idx].is_empty() {\n212\t        let evals = logup_outputs[trace_idx].to_host()?;\n213\t        // ... unzip frac, transpose, iDFT ...\n214\t        batch_sp_poly[2 * trace_idx] = numer_poly;\n215\t        batch_sp_poly[2 * trace_idx + 1] = denom_poly;\n216\t    }\n217\t}\n218\t```\n219\t\n220\t**Why**: After the explicit `cudaStreamSynchronize`, all kernels have completed and their output buffers are ready. The subsequent `to_host()` calls will perform near-instant D2H memcpy (no pending GPU work). The GPU pipeline was never stalled between kernel launches in Phase B.\n221\t\n222\t### Step 4: Keep original functions as wrappers (backward compatibility)\n223\t\n224\t**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/round0.rs`\n225\t\n226\tKeep `evaluate_round0_constraints_gpu` and `evaluate_round0_interactions_gpu` as convenience wrappers that allocate, launch, and return. They remain available for any other callers but are no longer used by the hot path.\n227\t\n228\t**Why**: Minimizes risk. Other code paths that use these functions are unaffected.\n229\t\n230\t## Invariants\n231\t\n232\t1. **Correctness**: Each AIR produces the same polynomial evaluations as before. The kernel inputs are identical; only the timing of D2H copies changes.\n233\t2. **Constraint kernel guard**: The zerocheck constraints kernel is launched only when `has_constraints == true`, which requires BOTH `!constraint_idx.is_empty()` AND `num_cosets_zc > 0`. This matches the existing guard at `round0.rs:46`. Note that `max_constraint_degree` (and thus `num_cosets_zc`) includes interaction expression degrees, so an AIR with interactions but no plain constraints can have `num_cosets_zc > 0` while having empty `constraint_idx`. Launching the zerocheck kernel on such an AIR would be incorrect.\n234\t3. **Intermediate buffer reuse**: On `cudaStreamPerThread`, kernels are serialized. The shared intermediate buffer is only accessed by one kernel at a time. Each kernel writes its output to a separate per-AIR DeviceBuffer.\n235\t4. **Memory safety**: Per-AIR output buffers are pre-allocated with the exact required capacity. Shared intermediate buffers are sized to the max across all AIRs. All buffers outlive the kernel launches (dropped after Phase C).\n236\t5. **Error handling**: If any kernel launch fails in Phase B, the error propagates immediately (before subsequent launches). CUDA runtime errors on the stream cause subsequent operations to fail, so partial failures are caught.\n237\t6. **Protocol unchanged**: The verifier is not modified. The same polynomials are produced; only the GPU execution order changes.\n238\t\n239\t## Measurement Plan\n240\t\n241\tRun the benchmark for APC 0, 100, 300 (using `run_pairing.sh` in the powdr repo):\n242\t```bash\n243\tcd /home/georg/powdr && openvm-riscv/scripts/run_pairing.sh\n244\t```\n245\t\n246\tAnalyze with `spec.py` and compare \"STARK (excl. trace)\" and its sub-components, particularly \"Round 0\":\n247\t```bash\n248\tpython3 /home/georg/spec.py results/pairing/apc000/metrics.json after_apc000\n249\tpython3 /home/georg/spec.py results/pairing/apc100/metrics.json after_apc100\n250\tpython3 /home/georg/spec.py results/pairing/apc300/metrics.json after_apc300\n251\t```\n252\t\n253\t**Expected outcomes (conservative estimate):**\n254\t- Round 0 at APC 300: from ~662ms to ~450-560ms (15-30% reduction). The saving comes from eliminating GPU idle time between kernel launches. The actual gain depends on how much of the 172ms overhead is GPU stall time vs. CPU post-processing (transpose/iDFT) that merely shifts from interleaved to post-batch.\n255\t- Round 0 at APC 0: roughly unchanged (only 99 AIRs, sync overhead is proportionally smaller)\n256\t- STARK excl trace at APC 300: from ~2455ms to ~2300-2400ms (~3-8% reduction)\n257\t- No regression in correctness (prove+verify passes)\n258\t\n259\t**Optimistic estimate** (if most overhead is GPU stall time, not CPU work):\n260\t- Round 0 at APC 300: ~350-450ms (30-50% reduction)\n261\t- STARK excl trace at APC 300: ~2150-2250ms (~10-15% reduction)\n262\t\n263\tAlso run nsight profiling for APC 300 to verify kernel pipelining:\n264\t```bash\n265\tnsys profile --output results/pairing/apc300/nsys_report --trace cuda,nvtx --sample none \\\n266\t  -- $PROVE_BIN prove --artifact apc300.cbor --input 0 --recursion\n267\t```\n268\t\n269\tLook for reduced gaps between kernel launches in the GPU timeline.\n270\t\n271\t## Rollback Criteria\n272\t\n273\t- Less than 10% improvement in Round 0 at APC 300 after full implementation\n274\t- Any correctness regression (prove fails or verify rejects)\n275\t- Peak GPU memory increases by more than 20% (unlikely given small output buffer overhead)\n276\t- Regression in APC 0 performance by more than 5%\n277\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6d64697b-3d86-45b2-9943-c4e9fc153ef4","uuid":"251478ea-7785-4237-9af8-1f7f331fda3c","timestamp":"2026-04-12T19:41:06.591Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/2026-04-12-2130-pipeline-round0-kernel-launches/plan.md","content":"# Plan: Pipeline Round 0 Kernel Launches\n\n## Goal\n\nEliminate per-AIR GPU synchronization in the Round 0 constraint evaluation loop to allow the GPU to execute kernels back-to-back without CPU stalls. This targets the largest sub-component regression in \"STARK excl. trace\": Round 0 increases from 178ms (APC 0, 99 AIRs) to 662ms (APC 300, 623 AIRs) despite a >2x reduction in total cells and constraints.\n\n## Current Code Path\n\nThe bottleneck is in `sumcheck_uni_round0_polys()` at `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs:598-884`.\n\n**Call chain (per AIR iteration, lines 732-880):**\n1. CPU: Prepare per-AIR data (constraints DAG, trace pointers, etc.)\n2. `evaluate_round0_constraints_gpu()` at `round0.rs:31-124`:\n   - Allocates `intermediates` (`DeviceBuffer::with_capacity`) — calls `cudaMallocAsync`\n   - Allocates `temp_sums_buffer` (`DeviceBuffer::with_capacity`) — calls `cudaMallocAsync`\n   - Allocates `sp_evals` output buffer\n   - Launches `zerocheck_ntt_eval_constraints` kernel via FFI\n   - Returns `sp_evals` DeviceBuffer (intermediates and temp_sums dropped = `cudaFreeAsync`)\n3. **SYNC**: `sum_buffer.to_host()` at `mod.rs:792` — `cudaMemcpyAsync` + `cudaEventSynchronize`\n4. CPU: Transpose, iDFT, polynomial construction → `batch_sp_poly[2*N + trace_idx]`\n5. `evaluate_round0_interactions_gpu()` at `round0.rs:132-275`:\n   - **CPU**: Builds `SymbolicDagBuilder`, encodes rules, computes numer/denom weights (lines 162-206)\n   - Uploads `d_rules`, `d_numer_weights`, `d_denom_weights` to GPU (3 H2D copies)\n   - Allocates `intermediates`, `temp_sums_buffer`, `s_evals` output buffer\n   - Launches `logup_bary_eval_interactions_round0` kernel via FFI\n   - Returns `s_evals` DeviceBuffer\n6. **SYNC**: `sum.to_host()` at `mod.rs:848` — `cudaMemcpyAsync` + `cudaEventSynchronize`\n7. CPU: Unzip frac, transpose, iDFT → `batch_sp_poly[2*i]`, `batch_sp_poly[2*i+1]`\n\n**Why this is slow with many AIRs:**\n- 623 AIRs × 2 sync points = 1,246 GPU synchronizations via `cudaEventSynchronize`\n- Each sync drains the GPU pipeline, preventing the next kernel from being submitted until the current one finishes AND the result is copied to host\n- CPU work between syncs (DAG construction, iDFT, etc.) blocks kernel submission\n- Per-AIR `cudaMallocAsync`/`cudaFreeAsync` for intermediates adds runtime API overhead\n- All work runs on `cudaStreamPerThread` (per-thread default stream), so operations are serialized\n\n**Profiling evidence (APC 300):**\n- Total GPU kernel time in Round 0: ~490ms (measured via nsight kernel summary)\n- Measured Round 0 wall time: 662ms\n- Overhead (sync stalls, CPU work, alloc): ~172ms (26% of wall time)\n- Key kernels: `zerocheck_ntt_evaluate_constraints_coset_parallel_kernel` (220ms, 539 instances), `logup_r0_ntt_eval_interactions_coset_parallel_kernel` (195ms + 29ms, 735 instances)\n\n## Changes\n\n### Step 1: Extract interaction preparation from `evaluate_round0_interactions_gpu`\n\n**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/round0.rs`\n\nCreate a new struct and function to pre-compute per-AIR interaction data:\n\n```rust\npub struct InteractionRound0Prep {\n    pub d_rules: DeviceBuffer<u128>,\n    pub d_numer_weights: DeviceBuffer<EF>,\n    pub d_denom_weights: DeviceBuffer<EF>,\n    pub denom_sum_init: EF,\n    pub buffer_size: u32,\n}\n```\n\nNote: The `SymbolicRulesGpu` is consumed during preparation (its `dag_idx_to_rule_idx` is used to map interaction expressions to rule indices for weight computation). Only the encoded device rules and computed weights survive into the struct. The `SymbolicDagBuilder` and its `expr_to_idx` map are also consumed during DAG construction and do not need to be stored.\n\nAdd function `prepare_round0_interactions(pk, symbolic, eq_3bs, beta_pows) -> Result<InteractionRound0Prep>` that extracts lines 161-212 from `evaluate_round0_interactions_gpu`. This performs:\n- DAG construction via `SymbolicDagBuilder` (CPU)\n- `SymbolicRulesGpu::new()` from the DAG (CPU)\n- Rule encoding: `rules.rules.iter().map(|c| c.encode()).collect_vec()` (CPU)\n- Weight computation: numer_weights, denom_weights, denom_sum_init using `rules.dag_idx_to_rule_idx` (CPU)\n- H2D upload of encoded rules (`d_rules`) and weights (`d_numer_weights`, `d_denom_weights`)\n\n**Why**: Separates CPU-heavy preparation from kernel launch, allowing all preparation to be done upfront before any kernel launches.\n\n### Step 2: Create kernel-launch-only variants of the evaluation functions\n\n**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/round0.rs`\n\nAdd two new functions that take pre-allocated buffers and launch kernels without allocating or syncing:\n\n```rust\npub fn launch_round0_constraints_kernel(\n    pk: &DeviceStarkProvingKey<...>,\n    // ... same params as current evaluate_round0_constraints_gpu ...\n    intermediates: &mut DeviceBuffer<F>,\n    temp_sums: &mut DeviceBuffer<EF>,\n    output: &mut DeviceBuffer<EF>,\n) -> Result<(), Round0EvalError>\n```\n\n```rust\npub fn launch_round0_interactions_kernel(\n    prep: &InteractionRound0Prep,\n    // ... trace pointers, eq_cube, etc ...\n    intermediates: &mut DeviceBuffer<F>,\n    temp_sums: &mut DeviceBuffer<Frac<EF>>,\n    output: &mut DeviceBuffer<Frac<EF>>,\n) -> Result<(), Round0EvalError>\n```\n\nThese functions call the same FFI (`zerocheck_ntt_eval_constraints`, `logup_bary_eval_interactions_round0`) but use externally-owned buffers instead of allocating their own. They do NOT perform D2H copies.\n\n**Why**: Decouples kernel launch from allocation and sync, enabling pipeline execution.\n\n### Step 3: Restructure the main loop in `sumcheck_uni_round0_polys`\n\n**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs` (lines 720-884)\n\nReplace the single per-AIR loop with three phases:\n\n**Phase A — Prepare (CPU, before any kernel launches):**\n```rust\n// Pre-compute per-AIR metadata\nlet mut per_air_data: Vec<Round0AirData> = Vec::with_capacity(num_present_airs);\nfor (trace_idx, ...) in izip!(...).enumerate() {\n    let single_pk = &self.pk.per_air[*air_idx];\n    let symbolic = SymbolicConstraints::from(&single_pk.vk.symbolic_constraints);\n    let local_deg = single_pk.vk.max_constraint_degree as usize;\n    let num_cosets_zc = local_deg.saturating_sub(1);\n    let num_cosets_logup = local_deg;\n\n    // IMPORTANT: max_constraint_degree includes interaction expression degrees.\n    // An AIR can have num_cosets_zc > 0 but no plain AIR constraints.\n    // We must check constraint_idx.is_empty() to determine if the zerocheck kernel\n    // should be launched, matching the guard at round0.rs:46.\n    let has_constraints = !single_pk.vk.symbolic_constraints.constraints.constraint_idx.is_empty()\n        && num_cosets_zc > 0;\n    \n    // Build interaction prep (currently done inside the loop at round0.rs:161-206)\n    let has_interactions = !eq_3bs.is_empty();\n    let interaction_prep = if has_interactions {\n        Some(prepare_round0_interactions(single_pk, &symbolic, eq_3bs, &self.beta_pows)?)\n    } else { None };\n    \n    // Compute main_parts, preprocessed_ptr (same as current lines 763-768)\n    let d_main_parts = ...;\n    \n    per_air_data.push(Round0AirData {\n        air_idx, n, height, local_deg, num_cosets_zc, num_cosets_logup,\n        has_constraints, has_interactions,\n        interaction_prep, d_main_parts, omega_root, eq_xi_ptr, ...\n    });\n}\n\n// Pre-allocate shared intermediate buffers (max size across all AIRs).\n// The sizing functions are thin wrappers over the existing unsafe FFI calls:\n//   _zerocheck_r0_intermediates_buffer_size(buffer_size, skip_domain, num_x, num_cosets, max_temp_bytes)\n//   _zerocheck_r0_temp_sums_buffer_size(buffer_size, skip_domain, num_x, num_cosets, max_temp_bytes)\n//   _logup_r0_intermediates_buffer_size(buffer_size, skip_domain, num_x, num_cosets, max_temp_bytes)\n//   _logup_r0_temp_sums_buffer_size(buffer_size, skip_domain, num_x, num_cosets, max_temp_bytes)\n// For zerocheck, buffer_size comes from pk.other_data.zerocheck_round0.inner.buffer_size.\n// For logup, buffer_size comes from InteractionRound0Prep.buffer_size.\nlet max_zc_intermed = per_air_data.iter().map(|d| zc_intermediates_size(d)).max().unwrap_or(0);\nlet max_zc_temp = per_air_data.iter().map(|d| zc_temp_size(d)).max().unwrap_or(0);\nlet max_logup_intermed = per_air_data.iter().map(|d| logup_intermediates_size(d)).max().unwrap_or(0);\nlet max_logup_temp = per_air_data.iter().map(|d| logup_temp_size(d)).max().unwrap_or(0);\nlet mut zc_intermediates = DeviceBuffer::with_capacity(max_zc_intermed.max(1));\nlet mut zc_temp_sums = DeviceBuffer::with_capacity(max_zc_temp.max(1));\nlet mut logup_intermediates = DeviceBuffer::with_capacity(max_logup_intermed.max(1));\nlet mut logup_temp_sums = DeviceBuffer::with_capacity(max_logup_temp.max(1));\n\n// Pre-allocate per-AIR output buffers (only for AIRs that will actually launch kernels)\nlet mut zc_outputs: Vec<DeviceBuffer<EF>> = per_air_data.iter()\n    .map(|d| if d.has_constraints { DeviceBuffer::with_capacity(d.num_cosets_zc * skip_domain) } else { DeviceBuffer::new() })\n    .collect();\nlet mut logup_outputs: Vec<DeviceBuffer<Frac<EF>>> = per_air_data.iter()\n    .map(|d| if d.has_interactions { DeviceBuffer::with_capacity(d.num_cosets_logup * skip_domain) } else { DeviceBuffer::new() })\n    .collect();\n```\n\n**Phase B — Launch all kernels (no sync):**\n```rust\nfor (trace_idx, data) in per_air_data.iter().enumerate() {\n    // Launch zerocheck constraint kernel ONLY if this AIR has plain constraints\n    // (has_constraints checks both constraint_idx.is_empty() and num_cosets_zc > 0)\n    if data.has_constraints {\n        launch_round0_constraints_kernel(\n            &self.pk.per_air[data.air_idx], data.selectors, &data.d_main_parts,\n            data.public_values, data.eq_xi_ptr, d_lambda_pows,\n            skip_domain, data.num_x, data.height, data.num_cosets_zc,\n            data.omega_root, max_temp_bytes,\n            &mut zc_intermediates, &mut zc_temp_sums, &mut zc_outputs[trace_idx],\n        )?;\n    }\n    // Launch logup interaction kernel if this AIR has interactions\n    if let Some(prep) = &data.interaction_prep {\n        launch_round0_interactions_kernel(\n            prep, data.selectors, &data.d_main_parts,\n            data.public_values, data.eq_xi_ptr,\n            skip_domain, data.num_x, data.height, data.num_cosets_logup,\n            data.omega_root, max_temp_bytes,\n            &mut logup_intermediates, &mut logup_temp_sums, &mut logup_outputs[trace_idx],\n        )?;\n    }\n}\n// All kernels submitted. No to_host() calls above.\n```\n\n**Phase C — Sync once + batch process results:**\n```rust\n// Explicit stream sync before D2H copies using the existing safe wrapper\n// (crates/cuda-common/src/stream.rs:81). This is cleaner than relying on the\n// first to_host()'s event sync and avoids the COPY_EVENT mutex for the initial wait.\ncurrent_stream_sync()?;\n\nfor (trace_idx, data) in per_air_data.iter().enumerate() {\n    // Process zerocheck output (same logic as current lines 791-826)\n    if !zc_outputs[trace_idx].is_empty() {\n        let q_evals = zc_outputs[trace_idx].to_host()?;\n        // ... transpose, iDFT, compute sp_0 ...\n        batch_sp_poly[2 * num_present_airs + trace_idx] = UnivariatePoly::new(coeffs);\n    }\n    // Process logup output (same logic as current lines 847-878)\n    if !logup_outputs[trace_idx].is_empty() {\n        let evals = logup_outputs[trace_idx].to_host()?;\n        // ... unzip frac, transpose, iDFT ...\n        batch_sp_poly[2 * trace_idx] = numer_poly;\n        batch_sp_poly[2 * trace_idx + 1] = denom_poly;\n    }\n}\n```\n\n**Why**: After the explicit `cudaStreamSynchronize`, all kernels have completed and their output buffers are ready. The subsequent `to_host()` calls will perform near-instant D2H memcpy (no pending GPU work). The GPU pipeline was never stalled between kernel launches in Phase B.\n\n### Step 4: Keep original functions as wrappers (backward compatibility)\n\n**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/round0.rs`\n\nKeep `evaluate_round0_constraints_gpu` and `evaluate_round0_interactions_gpu` as convenience wrappers that allocate, launch, and return. They remain available for any other callers but are no longer used by the hot path.\n\n**Why**: Minimizes risk. Other code paths that use these functions are unaffected.\n\n## Invariants\n\n1. **Correctness**: Each AIR produces the same polynomial evaluations as before. The kernel inputs are identical; only the timing of D2H copies changes.\n2. **Constraint kernel guard**: The zerocheck constraints kernel is launched only when `has_constraints == true`, which requires BOTH `!constraint_idx.is_empty()` AND `num_cosets_zc > 0`. This matches the existing guard at `round0.rs:46`. Note that `max_constraint_degree` (and thus `num_cosets_zc`) includes interaction expression degrees, so an AIR with interactions but no plain constraints can have `num_cosets_zc > 0` while having empty `constraint_idx`. Launching the zerocheck kernel on such an AIR would be incorrect.\n3. **Intermediate buffer reuse**: On `cudaStreamPerThread`, kernels are serialized. The shared intermediate buffer is only accessed by one kernel at a time. Each kernel writes its output to a separate per-AIR DeviceBuffer.\n4. **Memory safety**: Per-AIR output buffers are pre-allocated with the exact required capacity. Shared intermediate buffers are sized to the max across all AIRs. All buffers outlive the kernel launches (dropped after Phase C).\n5. **Error handling**: If any kernel launch fails in Phase B, the error propagates immediately (before subsequent launches). CUDA runtime errors on the stream cause subsequent operations to fail, so partial failures are caught.\n6. **Protocol unchanged**: The verifier is not modified. The same polynomials are produced; only the GPU execution order changes.\n\n## Measurement Plan\n\nRun the benchmark for APC 0, 100, 300 (using `run_pairing.sh` in the powdr repo):\n```bash\ncd /home/georg/powdr && openvm-riscv/scripts/run_pairing.sh\n```\n\nAnalyze with `spec.py` and compare \"STARK (excl. trace)\" and its sub-components, particularly \"Round 0\":\n```bash\npython3 /home/georg/spec.py results/pairing/apc000/metrics.json after_apc000\npython3 /home/georg/spec.py results/pairing/apc100/metrics.json after_apc100\npython3 /home/georg/spec.py results/pairing/apc300/metrics.json after_apc300\n```\n\n**Expected outcomes (conservative estimate):**\n- Round 0 at APC 300: from ~662ms to ~450-560ms (15-30% reduction). The saving comes from eliminating GPU idle time between kernel launches. The actual gain depends on how much of the 172ms overhead is GPU stall time vs. CPU post-processing (transpose/iDFT) that merely shifts from interleaved to post-batch.\n- Round 0 at APC 0: roughly unchanged (only 99 AIRs, sync overhead is proportionally smaller)\n- STARK excl trace at APC 300: from ~2455ms to ~2300-2400ms (~3-8% reduction)\n- No regression in correctness (prove+verify passes)\n\n**Optimistic estimate** (if most overhead is GPU stall time, not CPU work):\n- Round 0 at APC 300: ~350-450ms (30-50% reduction)\n- STARK excl trace at APC 300: ~2150-2250ms (~10-15% reduction)\n\nAlso run nsight profiling for APC 300 to verify kernel pipelining:\n```bash\nnsys profile --output results/pairing/apc300/nsys_report --trace cuda,nvtx --sample none \\\n  -- $PROVE_BIN prove --artifact apc300.cbor --input 0 --recursion\n```\n\nLook for reduced gaps between kernel launches in the GPU timeline.\n\n## Rollback Criteria\n\n- Less than 10% improvement in Round 0 at APC 300 after full implementation\n- Any correctness regression (prove fails or verify rejects)\n- Peak GPU memory increases by more than 20% (unlikely given small output buffer overhead)\n- Regression in APC 0 performance by more than 5%\n","numLines":277,"startLine":1,"totalLines":277}}}
